				le16_to_cpu(rom_desc->Size), buffer);
status = valid_csum(rom_desc, buffer);
Reason:
The `read_rom()` function copies `le16_to_cpu(rom_desc->Size)` bytes from the device into a fixed-size buffer of only 10 bytes (`sizeof(struct edge_ti_manuf_descriptor)`). The `Size` field is not validated against the buffer size; it is only checked against the maximum I2C size (16384 bytes). A malicious device can set `Size` to any value up to 16377, causing a heap overflow. Additionally, `valid_csum()` iterates over the same `Size` bytes in the buffer, compounding the out-of-bounds access.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
